# Cache-Control for static hosts that read a _headers file (Netlify,
# Cloudflare Pages). The real cache-control surface — fingerprinted URLs and
# meta tags do nothing without this. For nginx/Apache/Vercel/S3 recipes see the
# cache-busting skill's references/server-headers.md.
#
# Two-bucket model:
#   HTML          -> no-cache  (source of truth for which hashed assets to load)
#   hashed assets -> immutable (Vite content-hashes filenames; safe forever)

/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/cb-shapes/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
